# Cursor AI Instructions for ExplorationMinecraft Modpack Manager

## Code Structure Conventions
- Python scripts follow PEP 8 style guidelines
- Shell scripts follow Google's shell style guide
- Use descriptive variable and function names
- Comment complex logic and algorithms

## File Organization
- AISPEC/ - Technical documentation and AI reminders
- DOCS/ - User documentation, usage instructions, and architecture
- DEVJOURNAL/ - Development progress tracking with dated entries
- modpack_manager/ - Main application code
  - scripts/ - Shell scripts for management
  - modpack_profiles/ - Profile configuration files
  - modpack_cache/ - Downloaded mods
  - client_packs/ - Generated client-side modpacks

## Code Management
- Always check for dependencies in existing code before suggesting new libraries
- Prioritize Docker compatibility for all server components
- Maintain Python 2.7 compatibility while supporting Python 3+
- Handle API requests with proper error handling and retries
- Keep code modular and maintainable

## Project Goals
- Focus on user experience and simplicity in CLI interface
- Ensure robust mod dependency resolution
- Prioritize automation of tedious tasks
- Design for integration with Docker for server management 